Description: Build exr at opt-level 1, for reproducibility on arm64
 emeraldian intermittently fails to reproduce on arm64. LLVM allocates
 registers non-deterministically in exr's DWA decoder
 (exr::compression::dwa::lossy_dct::decode_lossy_channels), swapping x10 and
 x11 across four instructions with identical semantics. zola 0.23.6-4 works
 around the same function the same way. exr arrives through ratatui-image's
 image-defaults feature, and debian/rules asserts it is still in Cargo.lock.
 .
 A workaround, not a repair: drop it once LLVM fixes the non-determinism,
 confirmed over several builds on arm64.
Author: pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-28
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -57,6 +57,11 @@
 strip = true
 opt-level = 3
 
+# See debian/patches/deoptimise-exr-for-reproducibility.patch: LLVM's
+# register allocation in exr's DWA decoder varies between builds on arm64.
+[profile.release.package.exr]
+opt-level = 1
+
 # Dependencies are slow to compile but hot in the render loop; optimize them
 # even in debug builds so `cargo run` is still smooth at 60fps.
 [profile.dev.package."*"]
